1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,965
Nadia, Ethan,
thanks for coming in.

2
00:00:01,989 --> 00:00:05,392
Let's divide up the jobs for
the Sustainable Tourism Project.

3
00:00:06,079 --> 00:00:08,920
First, someone needs to get in
touch with the tour operators.

4
00:00:09,524 --> 00:00:12,160
Nadia, you've got contacts
from your internship, haven't you?

5
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:17,420
I have, but I'm away for two weeks
next month. Ethan, would you mind?

6
00:00:17,740 --> 00:00:20,340
Not at all.
I'll start ringing round this week.

7
00:00:20,700 --> 00:00:22,000
Then there's the questionnaire.

8
00:00:22,560 --> 00:00:26,300
That's the core of the whole project.
I wouldn't want to do it on my own.

9
00:00:26,540 --> 00:00:27,660
Let's do it together then.

10
00:00:28,010 --> 00:00:31,520
And the government reports?
There's a lot of policy detail in them.

11
00:00:31,685 --> 00:00:34,820
Leave those to me.
I studied tourism policy last year.

12
00:00:35,140 --> 00:00:36,140
What about the maps?

13
00:00:36,505 --> 00:00:39,680
Don't look at me.
I've never used the software.

14
00:00:40,080 --> 00:00:41,780
I have, so I'll do them.

15
00:00:42,075 --> 00:00:43,075
And the conclusion?

16
00:00:43,395 --> 00:00:44,960
Nadia's the better writer.

17
00:00:45,340 --> 00:00:47,500
Fine, but you're checking it.

18
00:00:47,820 --> 00:00:51,900
Now, your sources. The tourism
board website has some useful figures,

19
00:00:52,374 --> 00:00:54,302
but remember the
board exists to attract

20
00:00:54,326 --> 00:00:56,752
visitors, so it may not
give you the full picture.

21
00:00:57,215 --> 00:00:58,400
Be careful with its claims.

22
00:00:58,725 --> 00:01:00,820
What about the 2009 textbook?

23
00:01:01,260 --> 00:01:04,940
The industry has changed so much since
then that a lot of it no longer applies.

24
00:01:05,259 --> 00:01:06,460
And the article by Morrison?

25
00:01:06,939 --> 00:01:10,020
It's very good research, but
it's full of economic modelling,

26
00:01:10,629 --> 00:01:12,740
far more technical than
a project like yours needs.

27
00:01:13,079 --> 00:01:15,040
The International Travel Trends Survey?

28
00:01:15,399 --> 00:01:19,320
It covers the whole world, so it won't tell
you much about our region specifically.

29
00:01:19,749 --> 00:01:21,720
There's also a government database I found.

30
00:01:22,034 --> 00:01:24,880
That needs a licence, so don't rely on it.

31
00:01:25,314 --> 00:01:27,280
But last year's student
interviews are excellent.

32
00:01:27,739 --> 00:01:30,020
They asked almost exactly
the questions you're asking.

33
00:01:30,320 --> 00:01:31,155
Great!

34
00:01:31,179 --> 00:01:33,820
Right, your case studies. For overcrowding?

35
00:01:34,074 --> 00:01:36,940
Old Town is packed with
coach tours all summer.

36
00:01:37,259 --> 00:01:39,440
The Historic Centre. Yes, perfect.

37
00:01:40,130 --> 00:01:41,130
Eco-lodges?

38
00:01:41,184 --> 00:01:45,560
The National Park. All the new lodges
there are built from local materials.

39
00:01:46,005 --> 00:01:47,005
Local employment?

40
00:01:47,320 --> 00:01:48,320
The Coastal Town?

41
00:01:48,549 --> 00:01:50,000
They depend more on fishing there.

42
00:01:50,499 --> 00:01:52,487
In the Mountain
Village, almost everyone

43
00:01:52,511 --> 00:01:54,812
works in tourism, as
guides or in guesthouses.

44
00:01:55,260 --> 00:01:56,030
Transport?

45
00:01:56,054 --> 00:02:00,140
The island. There's only one
ferry and it can't cope in summer.

46
00:02:00,474 --> 00:02:01,660
And protecting wildlife?

47
00:02:02,119 --> 00:02:04,180
The Coastal Town might work after all.

48
00:02:04,479 --> 00:02:06,680
They've protected the
beaches where turtles nest.

49
00:02:06,994 --> 00:02:09,419
Good! That's a nice, positive example.

50
00:02:10,120 --> 00:02:11,240
Now, your timeline.

51
00:02:11,820 --> 00:02:14,280
Get the literature review
out of the way by week three.

52
00:02:14,640 --> 00:02:15,640
And the questionnaire?

53
00:02:16,830 --> 00:02:19,760
Have it ready by week five,
so there's time to pilot it.

54
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:22,060
Then the data collection in week seven?

55
00:02:23,100 --> 00:02:25,514
I'd originally said
seven, but you'll need

56
00:02:25,538 --> 00:02:28,312
ethics approval first,
so allow until week nine.

57
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:29,560
And the analysis?

58
00:02:30,750 --> 00:02:34,340
Two weeks after that, and the
first draft at the very end. Week 12.

59
00:02:34,730 --> 00:02:36,720
Thanks, this has really helped.

